{"id":"PPG_V2.80_beta1__compounds__cluster_values","collection":"PPG_V2.80_beta1","category":"compounds","source_path":"PPG_V2.80_beta1/compounds/cluster_values.json","root_names":["PPG::cluster_values"],"counts":{"nodes":59,"connections":103,"values":23,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Lets you build groups of values that are similar. Example: Face IDs must be grouped based on the Y-position of the face centers. - The face IDs are connected to Values to Cluster . - The Y component of the corresponding face centers is connected to Cluster Value . - All face IDs whose Y position is within the tolerance are grouped and output as a 2-dimensional array.","documentation_search":"Cluster Values Lets you build groups of values that are similar. Example: Face IDs must be grouped based on the Y-position of the face centers. - The face IDs are connected to Values to Cluster . - The Y component of the corresponding face centers is connected to Cluster Value . - All face IDs whose Y position is within the tolerance are grouped and output as a 2-dimensional array. - This can also be used for strings, identical strings are grouped together. Inputs Values to Cluster Array that you want to divide into groups. This can be any type. Cluster Value Array of scalar values or strings , same order as Values to Cluster . Values within 'Tolerance' (or equal strings) will be grouped together. Tolerance Values of the array Cluster Value are grouped if they differ no more than Tolerance . NOTE: this only works for numerical values of Cluster Value . Remainder Propagation Uses a \"smoother\" way to cluster numeric values. Instead of only using the difference between the first value in a group and the rest of the array, a \"remainder\" from the last group is taken into account, resulting in a more \"organic\" (i.e. irregular) grouping. NOTE: this only works for numerical values of Cluster Value . Descending Order Reverse the sorting of the Cluster Value . Outputs Clustered Values 2-dimensional array of all members of 'Values to Cluster'. Such a 2-dimensional array can be processed in a loop and also used with the node 'pattern rename'.","port_names":["cluster_value","clustered_values","descending_order","remainder_propagation","tolerance","values_to_cluster"],"node_types_search":["Core::Array::array_size","Core::Array::build_array","Core::Array::find_in_array","Core::Array::get_from_array","Core::Array::prefix_sum","Core::Array::resize_array","Core::Array::slice_array","Core::Array::sort_array_with_indices","Core::Logic::equal","Core::Logic::greater_or_equal","Core::Logic::if","Core::Math::absolute_value","Core::Math::decrement","Core::Math::max","Core::Math::subtract","Core::Type_Conversion::from_type_any","Core::Type_Conversion::to_bool","Core::Type_Conversion::to_double","Core::Type_Conversion::to_type_any","Unknown","cluster_scalars","cluster_strings","convert_to_double","split_the_value_array"],"dependencies_search":[],"roots":[{"overload_index":0,"name":"PPG::cluster_values","uri_imported":"stream:/bifrostGraphShape1","is_default_overload":null,"metadata":{"documentation":"../docs/ENU/cluster_values.md","_notes":[{"type":"sticky_note","text":"sort the array to bring similar values together"},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"resize \"cluster_values\" to match \"values_to_cluster"},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"strings are handled separate from scalar values.\n\"convert_to_double\" converts all scalar arrays (double, float, long, int, short, char, and unsigned) to double"},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"now build the clusters\n\"cluster lengths\" marks the length of each cluster"},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"now split the array \"values_to_cluster\" at those indices"},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"the cluster lengths are added up to become indices for a slice"}],"_sections":[{"type":"backdrop","title":"Split between scalar and string"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Safety"}]},"documentation_file":"PPG_V2.80_beta1/docs/ENU/cluster_values.md","documentation":"# Cluster Values\nLets you build groups of values that are similar.<br>\nExample: <br>\nFace IDs must be grouped based on the Y-position of the face centers.\n- The face IDs are connected to `Values to Cluster`.\n- The Y component of the corresponding face centers is connected to `Cluster Value`.\n- All face IDs whose Y position is within the tolerance are grouped and output as a 2-dimensional array.\n- This can also be used for strings, identical strings are grouped together.\n\n## Inputs\n\n### Values to Cluster\nArray that you want to divide into groups.<br>\nThis can be any type.\n\n### Cluster Value\nArray of `scalar values` or `strings`, same order as `Values to Cluster`.<br>\nValues within 'Tolerance' (or equal strings) will be grouped together.\n\t\n### Tolerance\nValues of the array `Cluster Value` are grouped if they differ no more than `Tolerance`.<br>\nNOTE: this only works for numerical values of `Cluster Value`.\n\n### Remainder Propagation\nUses a \"smoother\" way to cluster numeric values.<br>\nInstead of only using the difference between the first value in a group and the rest of the array, a \"remainder\" from the last group is taken into account, resulting in a more \"organic\" (i.e. irregular) grouping.<br>\nNOTE: this only works for numerical values of `Cluster Value`.\n\n### Descending Order\nReverse the sorting of the `Cluster Value`.\n\n## Outputs\n\n### Clustered Values\n2-dimensional array of all members of 'Values to Cluster'.<br>\nSuch a 2-dimensional array can be processed in a loop and also used with the node 'pattern_rename'.","ports":[{"name":"values_to_cluster","direction":"input","type":null},{"name":"cluster_value","direction":"input","type":null},{"name":"tolerance","direction":"input","type":null,"default":"0.100000001f"},{"name":"clustered_values","direction":"output","type":null},{"name":"remainder_propagation","direction":"input","type":"bool","default":"false"},{"name":"descending_order","direction":"input","type":"b